\description{
Standardises outcome model predictions under each named intervention and
reports pairwise causal contrasts (differences, ratios, or odds ratios)
with uncertainty estimates.

For all three causal estimators, \code{contrast()} computes E[Y^a] by setting
each individual's treatment to the intervened value and averaging the fitted
outcome model predictions over the target population. The target population
is controlled by \code{estimand} (or \code{subset} for subgroup effects). The
estimators differ only in how the outcome model was fitted; variance is
computed by the
\strong{unified influence-function engine} \code{variance_if()} (\code{R/variance_if.R}),
which handles all four cases (g-comp, IPW, matching, ICE) via one entry
point. See \code{vignettes/variance-theory.qmd} for the derivation and the
\code{R/variance_if.R} roxygen header for the architecture.
\itemize{
\item \code{"gcomp"}: standard \code{glm}/\code{gam} on the full data; one-model IF
correction via \code{prepare_model_if()} + \code{apply_model_correction()}.
\item \code{"ipw"}: density-ratio weighted MSM refit per intervention; IF
Channel 2 is the stacked-sandwich MSM-plus-propensity correction
assembled by \code{compute_ipw_if_self_contained_one()}, with the
cross-derivative \eqn{A_{\beta\alpha}} computed numerically by
\code{numDeriv::jacobian()}.
\item \code{"matching"}: \code{glm()} on the matched sample with match weights; IF is
computed on the matched sample and aggregated cluster-robustly on
\code{matched$subclass} via \code{vcov_from_if(cluster = ...)}.
}
}
\details{
\subsection{Estimands and standardisation}{

For each intervention \code{a}, \code{contrast()} evaluates the intervention function
on the target rows to obtain the intervened treatment vector
\eqn{a(L_i)}, then computes:

\deqn{E[Y^a] = (1/|S|) \sum_{i \in S} \hat{E}[Y | A = a(L_i), L_i]}
where \code{S} is the set of rows determined by the estimand:
\itemize{
\item \code{"ATE"}: all rows (full population)
\item \code{"ATT"}: rows where \code{A == 1} (observed treated)
\item \code{"ATC"}: rows where \code{A == 0} (observed controls)
\item \code{subset}: rows satisfying the quoted expression
}

For \code{"gcomp"}, one fit supports multiple estimands because the outcome
model is the same -- only the rows averaged over change. For \code{"ipw"} and
\code{"matching"}, the estimand is baked into the weights/matching and cannot
be changed after fitting.
}

\subsection{Estimand applicability}{\tabular{llll}{
   Treatment type \tab ATE \tab ATT/ATC \tab subset \cr
   Binary point \tab Yes \tab Yes \tab Yes \cr
   Continuous point \tab Yes \tab No (abort) \tab Yes \cr
   Categorical point \tab Yes \tab No (abort) \tab Yes \cr
   Multivariate point \tab Yes \tab No (abort) \tab Yes \cr
   Longitudinal \tab Yes \tab No (abort) \tab Yes \cr
}

}

\subsection{Treatment types and intervention support}{\tabular{lll}{
   Method \tab Treatment types \tab Intervention types \cr
   \code{"gcomp"} \tab binary, categorical, continuous, multivariate \tab all \cr
   \code{"ipw"} \tab binary, continuous \tab all deterministic \cr
   \code{"matching"} \tab binary \tab \code{static()} only \cr
}

}

\subsection{Variance estimation}{
\itemize{
\item \code{"sandwich"}: The unified influence-function engine \code{variance_if()}.
Per-individual IF = Channel 1 (direct covariate-sampling term) +
Channel 2 (one correction per nuisance model). Aggregated via
\code{vcov_from_if()}, with cluster-robust aggregation for matching.
Mathematically equivalent to the stacked M-estimation sandwich; see
\code{vignettes/variance-theory.qmd} Sections 3-4.
\item \code{"bootstrap"}: Resamples individuals (entire pipeline refitted \code{n_boot}
times). Respects cluster structure for longitudinal data.
\item The delta method is applied internally for ratio / odds-ratio
contrasts on top of the \code{"sandwich"} vcov; it is not a separate
\code{ci_method} option.
}
}
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
data("nhefs", package = "causatr")
fit <- causat(nhefs, outcome = "wt82_71", treatment = "qsmk",
              confounders = ~ sex + age + wt71)

# ATE: mean difference with sandwich SE
result <- contrast(fit,
  interventions = list(quit = static(1), continue = static(0)),
  type = "difference"
)

# ATT: override estimand in contrast() (gcomp only)
result_att <- contrast(fit,
  interventions = list(quit = static(1), continue = static(0)),
  estimand = "ATT"
)

# Subgroup effect: age > 50
result_sub <- contrast(fit,
  interventions = list(quit = static(1), continue = static(0)),
  subset = quote(age > 50)
)

# Continuous treatment: shift with NULL reference
fit_cont <- causat(nhefs, outcome = "wt82_71",
                   treatment = "smokeintensity",
                   confounders = ~ sex + age + wt71)
contrast(fit_cont,
  interventions = list(reduce10 = shift(-10), observed = NULL),
  type = "difference"
)

# Categorical treatment: three arms, reference = "radio"
contrast(fit_cat,
  interventions = list(chemo = static("A"), radio = static("B"),
                       combo = static("C")),
  type = "difference",
  reference = "radio"
)

# Stochastic intervention: random treatment assignment
sampler <- function(data, trt) {
  rbinom(nrow(data), 1, plogis(0.3 * data$age))
}
contrast(fit,
  interventions = list(
    stoch = stochastic(sampler, n_mc = 100L),
    always = static(1)
  ),
  type = "difference"
)
}

}
